Name the OpenHarmony version in a phone's User-Agent.

A phone sends Chrome's reduced Android User-Agent. Append the OpenHarmony
version as a product token, "... Mobile Safari/537.36 OpenHarmony/7.0",
so that sites looking for HarmonyOS find it while the platform section
stays exactly Chrome's: with "OpenHarmony 7.0" inside it, in front of the
Android token or after it, the phone failed Cloudflare Turnstile. The
version is the system's (OH_GetOSFullName), major.minor; the client hints
stay Android. Tablets and PCs are unchanged.

Generated against Chromium 154.0.8037.51 after chromium-154-harmonyos.patch.

Apply with:
  git -C /path/to/chromium/src apply /path/to/patches/ohos-phone-ua-openharmony.patch

diff --git a/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc b/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
--- a/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
+++ b/components/embedder_support/user_agent_utils.cc
@@ -294,9 +294,18 @@ std::string BuildOhosUserAgent(const std::string& product, bool mobile) {
   // to bot checks (Cloudflare Turnstile failed with 600010). The platform,
   // platform version, navigator.platform and navigator.plugins all follow
   // this string; see GetPlatformForUAMetadata() below.
+  //
+  // With the OpenHarmony version as a product token at the end, as in
+  // "... Mobile Safari/537.36 OpenHarmony/7.0": sites that look for HarmonyOS
+  // find it, and the platform section stays exactly Chrome's -- with
+  // "OpenHarmony 7.0" inside it, before or after the Android token, the
+  // phone failed Cloudflare Turnstile. The client hints stay Android.
   return base::StrCat({"Mozilla/5.0 (Linux; Android 10; K) AppleWebKit/537.36 "
                        "(KHTML, like Gecko) ",
-                       product, " Mobile Safari/537.36"});
+                       product, " Mobile Safari/537.36",
+                       major_minor.empty()
+                           ? std::string()
+                           : base::StrCat({" OpenHarmony/", major_minor})});
 }
 #endif  // BUILDFLAG(IS_OHOS)
 
